cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Task-Aware Token Budget Forecasting for Agentic Workflows"
message: >-
  If you use this code or refer to our work, please cite the manuscript
  (preferred-citation below) and this repository.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Harish
    family-names: Gaggar
    affiliation: Intuit Inc.
    email: harish_gaggar@intuit.com
abstract: >-
  TABF forecasts per-stage token use from a task description alone;
  ContextOptimizer trims the live message list before each LLM call while
  preserving tool-call/response structure. This repository contains the
  benchmark, experiments, and artifacts for the accompanying paper.
keywords:
  - context engineering
  - token budget forecasting
  - LLM agents
  - agentic workflows
  - cost optimisation
  - gradient boosting
repository-code: "https://github.com/harish-gaggar/agentic-token-budget-forecast"
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Task-Aware Token Budget Forecasting for Agentic Workflows"
  authors:
    - given-names: Harish
      family-names: Gaggar
  year: 2026
  notes: "Manuscript and BibTeX in paper.tex / paper.bib; update with venue DOI when published."
